### The three remaining sorries — why they are blocked by the frozen signatures (no statement weakened, none false)

1. **`variance_rbEstimator_le_of_complete`** (LehmannScheffe minimality). `IsUMVU`'s minimality quantifies over competitors `δ'` carrying only `MemEstL2 P δ'` — i.e. a *per-parameter* `AEStronglyMeasurable` representative, **no global `Measurable δ'`**. The kernel Rao–Blackwell comparison (`variance_rbEstimator_le`) needs `Measurable δ'`, and the completeness step needs the θ-free certificate `t ↦ ∫ δ' dQ_t` to be genuinely `Measurable` with identically-zero mean. These do not glue to one global measurable representative (false in general — Dirac families are a counterexample), and `IsCompleteStat` demands `Measurable`. Closing it needs a `condExp`-based RB layer (integrability-only), which is not among the imported kernel lemmas. The theorem is **true**, just unreachable with this API + frozen hypotheses.

2. **`isUMVU_of_fullRank_expFamily`**. It must feed `HasSufficientKernel P E.stat` (the graph/compProd kernel) into `isUMVU_of_complete_sufficient`. The only route to that kernel, `Sufficiency.RegularConditional.hasSufficientKernel_of_isSufficient`, requires `[StandardBorelSpace 𝓧]` (+ `[Nonempty 𝓧]`) — **absent from the frozen signature**, and an exponential family gives no explicit reconstruction kernel over an abstract measurable space. (Completeness itself transfers fine.)

3. **`isMinimalSufficient_stat`**. Two obstacles: (i) the sufficiency half routes through `Sufficiency.Factorization.isSufficient_of_isFactorizedDensity`, which is **itself an open `sorry` in this worktree** (I may not edit it); (ii) the minimality half is a substantial likelihood-ratio-inversion + Doob–Dynkin (`Measurable.exists_eq_measurable_comp`) development beyond the imported API.

### Note on the escape-hatch budget
The "≤1 lifted private sorry per file" was met for `MinimalSufficient` (1) but **exceeded in `LehmannScheffe` (2)**. I could not satisfy it without either weakening a statement (forbidden) or fabricating a proof: the two LS gaps are independent, each forced by a distinct missing hypothesis in a frozen signature (non-`Measurable` competitor; missing `StandardBorelSpace`). I chose to leave both statements exactly as posed and document the precise obstruction at each `sorry`.

No statement was weakened; no unproven content was laundered into hypotheses; nothing outside the three target files was edited.
